<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Béla IV of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1206–1270</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Béla IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was king from 1235 to 1270. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> crushed his army at Mohi in 1241 and devastated Hungary, forcing him to flee to the Adriatic. After their withdrawal he rebuilt the kingdom, encouraging stone castles, fortified towns and settlers, and is remembered as Hungary's second founder. In 1247 he granted the Banate of Severin to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bela-iv-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Béla IV of Hungary" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_126.oldal_-_IV._B%C3%A9la_uralkod%C3%B3i_d%C3%ADszben.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
